# Operator credentials for suprstar.
#
# Copy this file to ops/.env.ops and fill in the values with your editor.
# ops/.env.ops is gitignored. Do not paste these values into a chat: put them
# here and they get read from disk instead.
#
#   cp ops/.env.ops.example ops/.env.ops
#   chmod 600 ops/.env.ops
#   open -e ops/.env.ops      # or use any editor
#
# Then check they all work, without any value being printed:
#
#   bash ops/check.sh

# --- Render (hosts the API) -------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Account Settings → API Keys → Create API Key
RENDER_API_KEY=
RENDER_SERVICE_ID=srv-dan09njtqb8s73a3v5s0

# --- Vercel (hosts the client) ----------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Account Settings → Tokens → Create
VERCEL_TOKEN=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=prj_v4zmwaN7fBgZLtxzPkcpKtPXHU3k

# --- Microsoft Entra ID (sign-in) -------------------------------------------
# App registration in the Entra admin center: single tenant, redirect URI
# https://suprstar.social/api/auth/entra/callback (plus
# http://localhost:5173/api/auth/entra/callback for development). No API
# permissions need adding: openid, profile and email are delegated defaults.
# Push these onto Render with: bash ops/set-signin-env.sh
ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
ENTRA_TENANT_ID=
ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Mail (magic links + access-request notices) ----------------------------
# Fill all three together: a provider without its key leaves magic links dark.
# MAIL_PROVIDER is "resend" or "smtp". For smtp, set SMTP_URL instead of RESEND_API_KEY.
MAIL_PROVIDER=
MAIL_FROM=
RESEND_API_KEY=
SMTP_URL=

# --- GitHub -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing goes here. Git already reads the token from the macOS keychain, and
# it can be read back programmatically without ever being displayed. To replace
# it, run these two lines yourself in a terminal (substituting your token):
#
#   printf "protocol=https\nhost=github.com\n" | git credential-osxkeychain erase
#   printf "protocol=https\nhost=github.com\nusername=jameschrisa\npassword=NEW_TOKEN\n\n" | git credential-osxkeychain store
#
# Give the new token "workflow" scope (classic) or Workflows: Read and write
# (fine-grained) so the CI workflow can be pushed.
